// How items sit in a survivor's hand (read by the client: crates/client/src/held.rs).
//
// Anything held is drawn in the hand's grip frame, which is fixed on the hand (the thing follows
// the hand, and the hand closes round it): the grip at the origin, on the palm (4 cm out of the
// hand's middle, where the closed fingers go round it); the item pointing along +Z, out past the
// thumb; its top +Y, toward the wrist; so +X is out of the right palm, and for the left hand out
// of its back. Three ways of holding (`survivor_model::Hold`):
//   - a handle (a weapon that isn't a gun, anything with a held model), in a hammer grip: at rest
//     +Z runs across the palm, 45 degrees off the knuckles' line toward the fingers, so it points
//     forward and down from a hanging hand; along the knuckles while a guard or a blow has the arm;
//   - a gun: its barrel (+Z) on the way the fingers point, its top (+Y) to the thumb;
//   - a small thing in the fist (everything else): +Z along the knuckles' line. A thing that stands
//     (a mug, a tin, a bottle) is put upright in the fist, its top to +Z; a flat one along +Z, flat
//     on the palm; either with its middle on the grip, as far out of the palm as it is thick.
// A held model is made that way. A grip here then moves the item in that frame (`offset`, metres),
// turns it (`turn`, degrees about X, then Y, then Z) and scales it (`scale`), so an item that sits
// wrong is put right without code. Every field is optional.
//
// `carry` is how the thing is carried while nothing else has the arm (standing, walking, running,
// sneaking; `held::Carry`, `SurvivorModel::carry`):
//   - Side: the arm hangs and swings as the body's clips have it (the default for a weapon);
//   - Front: the elbow bent, the forearm forward at the waist, the thing upright in the fist in
//     front of the body (the default for everything else: a mug, a tin, a bottle);
//   - Low: low and ready at the side, the forearm forward and down 30 degrees, clear of the thigh.
// A guard, a blow, eating, drinking, a reload, a gesture and so on take the arm from the carry.
//
// A release build's models have grips of their own (release-models/held/grips.ron), read over
// these, since a grip belongs to the model it fits.
//
//   "kitchen_knife": (offset: (0.0, 0.0, -0.02), turn: (0.0, 0.0, 90.0), scale: 1.0),
//
// Two entries are not items: "eating" and "drinking" are put on top of the grip of the food or
// drink in use, in the left hand's frame (+X out of the back of that hand), while the clip has the
// fist at the face: they bring the thing to the lips.
{
    // A pistol at rest is held low and ready, its barrel forward and down, not down the leg.
    "pistol": (carry: Low),
    // A flashlight too, and turned 60 degrees in the fist, toward the fingers, to shine ahead.
    "flashlight": (carry: Low, turn: (60.0, 0.0, 0.0)),
    // Too big to hold up in one fist.
    "log": (carry: Side),
    "petrol_can": (carry: Side),
    // The eating clip holds the fist in front of the mouth, thumb up, palm to the face: the food in
    // the fingers (not out past the knuckles), a little out of the palm and down, tipped to the mouth.
    "eating": (offset: (0.02, 0.0, -0.05), turn: (0.0, -20.0, 0.0)),
    // The drinking clip holds the fist in front of the brow, thumb to the face: the bottle tipped up
    // through the fist, its neck down at the lips, its base up and out in front.
    "drinking": (offset: (-0.01, 0.0, 0.01), turn: (-27.0, -20.0, 0.0)),
}
